<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#FFFFFF', padding: '60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
  <Box style={{ height: 64, background: '#1E4FA8', flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', justifyContent: 'space-between', paddingLeft: 24, paddingRight: 24 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Not an artefact of one seed or one algorithm</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#FFFFFF', opacity: 0.8 }}>06 · Validation</Text>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ marginTop: 30, flexDirection: 'row', gap: 44 }}>
    <Box style={{ width: 380, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 12 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', letterSpacing: 1 }}>STABILITY</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 72, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1 }}>0.979</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>mean adjusted Rand index between the reference partition and 30 bootstrap resamples of the 200 records (sd 0.025).</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>A partition learned from a perturbed sample is almost identical to the one reported — the groups are properties of the population, not of the sample.</Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 10 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', letterSpacing: 1 }}>AGREEMENT WITH OTHER ALGORITHMS</Text>
      <Table
        style={{ width: '100%', height: 232 }}
        defaultTextStyle={{ fontSize: 16, textAlign: 'left', color: '#1A2230' }}
        defaultCellStyle={{ border: { bottom: { width: 1, color: '#D6DCE5' } }, padding: '6px 8px' }}
        cells={[
          [
            { text: 'Algorithm', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#1E4FA8' } },
            { text: 'Clusters', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right', bold: true, color: '#1E4FA8' } },
            { text: 'ARI vs. K-Means', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right', bold: true, color: '#1E4FA8' } },
          ],
          ['K-Means, k = 5 (reference)', { text: '5', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }, { text: '1.000', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right', bold: true } }],
          ['Gaussian mixture, full covariance', { text: '5', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }, { text: '0.957', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }],
          ['Agglomerative, Ward linkage', { text: '5', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }, { text: '0.942', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }],
          ['Bisecting K-Means', { text: '5', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }, { text: '0.659', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }],
          ['DBSCAN (eps = 0.47, minPts = 5)', { text: '2', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right' } }, { text: '0.273', textStyle: { textAlign: 'right', color: '#D9534F' } }],
        ]}
      />
    </Box>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ marginTop: 26, background: '#E8EFF8', borderLeft: '4px solid #1E4FA8', padding: '18px 24px' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>Three methods with different inductive biases find the same five groups. DBSCAN cannot: the groups are separated by <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>gaps of varying width</span>, so no single radius isolates five of them — a failure that explains itself.</Text>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 610, left: 0, width: 1160, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>Mall Customer Segmentation · Course Project</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>06 / 11</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
